            <ArticleTitle>Atypical CML with massive splenic infarct: an extremely rare presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2015-212821</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2015212821</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 47-year-old man who presented with hepatosplenomegaly, anaemia and massive splenic infarct. A series of investigations led us to a diagnosis of atypical chronic myeloid leucaemia, a rare variety of a mixed myelodysplastic/myeloproliferative neoplasm. This is the first case of atypical CML presenting with massive splenic infarction.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
